{
  "$comment": [
    "PLATO JSON-LD 1.1 context: maps every key of plato.schema.json and of the two submission profiles to its term in https://w3id.org/plato#, so that expanding a conformant submission yields the RDF graph the ontology describes. Intended URL: https://w3id.org/plato/schemas/plato.context.jsonld.",
    "Written against ontology.ttl at owl:versionInfo 0.7.1. How it got there: first written against 0.4.0 plus the unreleased additions up to commit 915cf7f; revised after it so that a gazetteer's title and licence map to dcterms:title and dcterms:license (a Gazetteer is a dcat:Dataset), not to plato:authority_title and plato:licence, whose domains made every Gazetteer an Authority. The note on authorityType defaults was added after the same review. A later revision added ccodes (plato:ccodes) on SpatialEntities. A later revision mapped relationLabel to plato:source_label and removed metaTypeLabel. A later one added sourceLabel on names, geometries and timespans, certaintyLevel (plato:certainty_level) wherever certainty applies, and entityIdentifier and namespace on SpatialEntities. A later one added transcriptionAccuracy and transcriptionCompleteness on every facet, negated on attestations and citationFunction on citations. A later one added the gazetteer’s version, status, isVersionOf and previousVersion (DCAT 3 and plato:gazetteer_status). A later one added dataSets, dataSet, dimensions, attributes and universe for statistical figures. For 0.6.0, sourceStance on attestations and licence on sources; computed wherever certainty applies; relatedLabel on relations; duration on timespans; and relationTypes, the relation types a document declares (plato:declares_relation_type). For 0.7.0, creator, keywords, spatial, temporal, landingPage and uriSpace on the gazetteer (DCAT, Dublin Core, FOAF and VoID terms, no new PLATO ones); identities on attestations (plato:attests_identity); and scheme and schemeVersion on types (skos:inScheme, plato:scheme_version). Verified for 0.5.0 by expanding the repository's four JSON examples and six DEEP/EPNS place-centric documents, and for 0.6.0, 0.7.0 and 0.7.1 by expanding its ten JSON examples: every term declared, every schema key a context term, no node in two unrelated classes. Update this line when the context changes.",
    "Reading the profiles: the document node is the Gazetteer ('gazetteer' is nested into it), and its top-level arrays are contains_entity / contains_attestation / contains_identity_relation. In place-centric documents an attestation nested under a spatialEntity is linked by the reverse of attests_about, and an identity relation nested there by the reverse of identity_subject, so neither needs 'about' or 'subject'. 'qualification', 'relations' and 'meta' are nesting keys: their contents are properties of the enclosing node. Where one JSON key means different things by parent ('label', 'source', 'contributor', 'identifier'), a property-scoped context resolves it.",
    "Known limits of a context, which a triplifier must cover itself: (1) no rdf:type is added to attestation, name, geometry, timespan, type, propertyValue, spatialEntity, citation or identityRelation objects; the ontology's domains and ranges let a reasoner infer them. authorityType on a source object does become rdf:type, but only where it is stated: the schema's default of 'source' is not applied by JSON-LD, so an omitted authorityType leaves an Authority of no stated kind. State it when RDF is the target. (2) timespan bounds are left untyped strings; type them by shape (xsd:gYear, xsd:date, xsd:dateTime) if a store is to index them. (3) reprPoint and bbox become RDF lists of numbers, not the WKT literals the ontology declares. (4) propertyValue.value is mapped to value_literal; a structured value should be serialised into value_json by the producer. (5) name strings carry no language tag; the producer may add one from 'language'. (6) gazetteer.contributor and identityRelation.assertedBy are coerced to IRIs, so give a URI, not a bare name; contributorObject.affiliation is not coerced, so a free-text affiliation becomes a literal on contributor_affiliation.",
    "Anything the context does not name is dropped silently on expansion. Keep this file in step with plato.schema.json: a key added there must be added here.",
    "Statistical figures (issue #14): dataSets in the header maps to dcterms:hasPart of qb:DataSet nodes, with their structures; on a propertyValue, dataSet maps to qb:dataSet, universe to plato:universe, and dimensions and attributes are nesting keys whose absolute-IRI keys become the observation's own dimension and attribute statements, as JSON-LD expands such keys."
  ],
